\begin{proof}
Suppose that $H$ is a subgroup of $G$ with $|H|=n-1$, where $n=|G|>2$. By Lagrange's theorem, $|H|$ divides $|G|$, so $n-1$ divides $n$. Hence $n-1$ divides $n-(n-1)=1$, which implies $n-1=1$ and therefore $n=2$, contradicting $n>2$. Thus $G$ cannot have such a subgroup.
\end{proof}

